-- title:
--   Affine evaluation commutes with reduction to a divisor modulus
-- statement:
--   Let $p,D\in\mathbb N$ with $p\mid D$, and let $\psi$ be an integer affine form on a finite variable set. For a vector $x$ over $\mathbb Z/D\mathbb Z$, reducing its affine evaluation by the canonical homomorphism to $\mathbb Z/p\mathbb Z$ equals evaluating $\psi$ after reducing every coordinate. Positivity and primality of the moduli are not assumed.
